  "cross_validation": "2-impl interop: AlgoVoi rfc8785@0.1.4 (Python) and EPI Recorder, byte-identical frame_ids on 2026-06-11. The canonical FORM also agrees byte-for-byte where EPI publishes a canonical_json (Mueller / non-ASCII case included).",
  "timestamp_note": "These inputs carry EPI-form ISO-8601 string timestamps (or none) and are NOT substrate-timestamp-compliant: the substrate requires integer-millisecond timestamps and rejects RFC 3339 / ISO-8601 strings (draft-hopley-x402-canonicalisation-jcs-v1 section 4.1). They are interop fixtures pinning the JCS RFC 8785 + SHA-256 canonicalisation method, where both implementations produce identical frame_ids over the literal input bytes. Each vector declares its timestamp_encoding so the boundary is testable. Substrate-native epoch-millisecond variants may be added later as a separate labelled set.",
  "verification_recipe": [
    "1. Take input verbatim.",
    "2. Canonicalise with RFC 8785.",
    "3. base64-encode the JCS bytes; it MUST equal expected_jcs_bytes_b64.",
    "4. SHA-256 the JCS bytes, lowercase hex, prefix 'sha256:'; it MUST equal frame_id."
  ],
